  "body": "```js\r\nalert('U+0009 TAB\\u0009U+000B VT\\u000BU+000C FF\\u000CSome more text');\r\n```\r\n\r\n- Gecko: a few spaces for TAB, boxed four-digit codes for VT and FF\r\n- Blink: empty boxes (tofu) for TAB and VT; an up arrow (!) for FF\r\n- Edge: a decent amount of spaces for TAB; newlines for VT and FF\r\n- WebKit: a single space for TAB; newlines for VT and FF\r\n\r\nI'm not sure how much effort we should devote to getting interop here... if we wanted to do this properly we should probably also be testing control characters and Unicode line separators. A lot of work, but do people care? Personally I think I'll try to finish up https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/4105 and just leave the rest of this as documenting a non-interop, for someone else to finish...\r\n\r\n/cc @avidrissman",
